        {
          "id": 817395626,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Good point. That's what the offset column says in the document(*). However the format of that field as stated in the document is:\n\n```\n   |  8  |  7  |  6  |  5  |  4  |  3  |  2  |  1  |\n   -------------------------------------------------\n   |spare|spare|spare|spare|         NSAPI         |\n   -------------------------------------------------\n```\n\nSo, I'm not seeing how this spans two octets. \n\nAlso when looking at the definition of NSAPI it's stated to be a \"integer value in the range [0;15]\", so that fits the figure too.\n\nFurthermore, no other IE has an NSAPI field larger then one octet. \n\nAlso the text in the document for this IE speaks of the NSAPI in singular form.\n\nAnd since there are Editor notes in the document, also for this IE, I assume this is quite new.\n\nAnd the sample capture provided in issue #17869 has a single octet allocated for this.\n\nConsidering all this I took the guess that the offset is not giving the real picture here and went for a single octet for this field.\n\n(*)3GPP TS 29.060 V17.1.0",
          "author": {
            "id": 2398962,
            "username": "JaapKeuter",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Jaap Keuter",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/722b0c520542a23cb8f8ea7070a45c88f9e9214dc700ac151e419e9649e0304e?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/JaapKeuter"
          },
